<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump admin's hardline deportation policy an 'attempt to break the global refugee and asylum system'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c58877c94aefe6e920d8089d4e22bc9297d60f935a85cb9602ed37c5b5da7265</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T11:28:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260922-trump-admin-s-hardline-deportation-policy-an-attempt-to-break-the-global-refugee-and-asylum-system" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Washington Post national security reporter Adam Taylor. The Forbidden Stories consortium, involving France 24 and 25 other media outlets, has spent six months investigating the thousands of people abruptly deported from the United States to third countries, amid concerns over due process and their ability to challenge their removal. The investigation examines how the Trump administration has made deportation a major focus of both US immigration and foreign policy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Top TV networks – including Fox – revolt in solidarity with media banned by Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9272900c59558a002a6ad26c410fa02c72230efddc8a366385fb26417a47fb4b</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:59:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-top-tv-networks-%E2%80%93-including-fox-%E2%80%93-revolt-in-solidarity-with-media-banned-by-trump" /><summary type="html">The top five US television networks staged a revolt on Monday when they effectively boycotted coverage of President Donald Trump to protest his decision to ban three news outlets from the White House. "No administration should restrict a news organization because it objects to its reporting," ABC, CBS, CNN, Fox and NBC said in a joint statement.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump: US outlets boycott Trump over media ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8366a14ce103426a990fc392a114ada503f8ea64a7913bbd79f4313506fe096</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:53:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-donald-trump-us-outlets-boycott-trump-over-media-ban" /><summary type="html">During a ribbon-cutting ceremony for a new helipad at the White House on Monday, Donald Trump made a brief statement that was inaudible.
 
In response to Trump’s decision to bar MS NOW, CNN and Politico from the White House, US television networks, including ABC, CBS, NBC and Fox News, suspended their pooled coverage of the president.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Guterres calls for UN Security Council reform</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d4242518315ea23b5e0e2ac09e6b216b7ef0532b12360f847712044d8247f0c</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:09:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate" /><summary type="html">UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres opened the General Assembly in New York on Tuesday for the last time before his term ends on December 31. Guterres will be followed at the podium by Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, US President Donald Trump and French President Emmanuel Macron. Watch his address live on FRANCE 24.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>World leaders gather at UN amid wars, AI fears and global divisions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:778747701887d4933ee4e9eac3e95531b6001ec77ab923b0941e7b210be9a95a</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T03:49:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-world-leaders-gather-at-un-amid-wars-ai-fears-and-global-divisions--d1ee36515d6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-world-leaders-gather-at-un-amid-wars-ai-fears-and-global-divisions" /><summary type="html">World leaders are gathering at the United Nations this week against a backdrop of wars in the Middle East and Ukraine, rising fears over artificial intelligence and mounting economic and climate pressures. The annual General Assembly will test whether the 193-member body can still bring countries together to tackle crises that increasingly transcend borders.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US, Denmark and Greenland to sign security deal on Tuesday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:308e8418fa69a7478bca6c99f9a9a94fd3b49df3a2e6bf1e25a6bde2868010c4</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T23:30:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-denmark-and-greenland-to-sign-security-deal-on-tuesday--e3730ada4f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-denmark-and-greenland-to-sign-security-deal-on-tuesday" /><summary type="html">The United States, Denmark and Greenland are set to sign a security agreement Tuesday expanding US involvement in Greenland’s defence while affirming Danish sovereignty over the Arctic territory.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount settles with US states, clearing path for Warner Bros. merger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8ca34573cd976217c9eda3e00a1c08849dcf8f2c67e845aa45c54694263cd28</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T22:48:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-paramount-settles-with-us-states-clearing-path-for-warner-bros-merger--f9c2a041c5b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-paramount-settles-with-us-states-clearing-path-for-warner-bros-merger" /><summary type="html">Paramount has reached a settlement with California and 11 other states that clears a major legal hurdle to its $110 billion takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery, with the deal imposing commitments on film production, jobs and editorial independence at CNN and CBS News.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran hit by viral false claims after Macklemore controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f644f299b949950a221babf755ac9cc24c125a8c6cf067b2addf8ad22fc30a1d</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T21:05:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-hit-by-viral-false-claims-after-macklemore-controversy-1--cd1d21c7e597.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-hit-by-viral-false-claims-after-macklemore-controversy-1" /><summary type="html">Ed Sheeran's controversial US tour has sparked a wave of viral rumours. A false claim that his music was removed from Spotify racked up more than 3 million views on X, despite his music remaining available. Another video, viewed over 14 million times, falsely suggested Sheeran was now defiantly performing solo after all his support acts withdrew. But not only is the footage dated, Sheeran has in fact replaced the backing musicians. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Banking on a national brand': Bolsonaro sons Carlos, Jair Renan run for power in Brazil's south</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aac486af8f8bd5fc41b62b97223bf176fe93d0e36c5c309777027c08077411f5</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T17:46:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-bolsonaro-sons-carlos-and-race-for-power-brazil-south--3d3858e0bb77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-bolsonaro-sons-carlos-and-race-for-power-brazil-south" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro is not the only member of his family campaigning in his father’s shadow. The former president's eldest son, who is now polling neck and neck with incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, can count on two of his brothers, who are standing in the senatorial and legislative elections. In Santa Catarina, one of Brazil’s most pro-Bolsonaro southern states, their surname alone is enough to secure victory.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico to sue Trump administration after White House ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3f0b8d845c3011de1a6d7473f8b3726cb6469d9904468d5658cde5102042c74</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:34:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-cnn-ms-now-politico-sue-trump-administration-after-white-house-ban--1eae5b26a76f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-cnn-ms-now-politico-sue-trump-administration-after-white-house-ban" /><summary type="html">US media outlets CNN, MS NOW and Politico announced Monday they were filing suit after US President Donald Trump banned their journalists from the White House last week. The ban on the three outlets marks an escalation in the Trump administration's years-long assault on the country's press freedoms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Midterm elections: Trump looms large over 2026 vote as Democrats eye gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ee8b42d04a912f2b93d69cdbb00da8a690f756caedd63f2b305ceef28b04512</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T12:51:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/midterm-elections-trump-looms-large-over-2026-vote-as-democrats-eye-gains--8893a9a014d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/midterm-elections-trump-looms-large-over-2026-vote-as-democrats-eye-gains" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections now just six weeks away, we’ll speak to our Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson about whether President Donald Trump could help or hurt his party’s chances. Polls have pointed to what some are calling a “blue wave”, with Democrats potentially regaining control of the House, while the Senate race remains more uncertain. Trump has ramped up campaigning, including spending heavily on advertising and proposing $5,000 payments to voters who support Republicans. But with his approval ratings under pressure amid the war in Iran and the Middle East, and rising oil, gasoline and commodity prices compared with before he took office, the political landscape could still shift significantly in the coming weeks.</summary></entry><entry><title>Protests erupt after ICE shooting in Texas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b09ed8fced30da74fcde58d3f4c2819111d540f62793d74b8b9f3f6ce1bda60</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T09:03:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/protests-erupt-after-ice-shooting-in-texas--235cc568ff71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/protests-erupt-after-ice-shooting-in-texas" /><summary type="html">Protests have broken out in Austin, Texas, after a US Immigration and Customs Enforcement officer shot and wounded a man during a traffic stop. The man remains in serious but stable condition in hospital, while anti-ICE protesters quickly gathered at the scene. Austin’s police chief said local officers were not involved in the shooting. Ellen Gainsford reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Colombia battles massive wildfire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44f4b011d34b3dc37d5a4da5f39a7a04c2e197bcb9a513197e84d18bf75f31d9</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T09:00:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/colombia-battles-massive-wildfire--3e4a063c1c7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/colombia-battles-massive-wildfire" /><summary type="html">Colombia’s disaster risk agency says a forest fire in the centre of the country is now partially under control. Around 250 firefighters, supported by volunteers, have been battling the blaze since Saturday, with some 200 hectares affected. Camille Corcoran takes a closer look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Deportation project: 72 journalists investigate US treatment of migrants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7461370e5d8dabd5d0bec68c7043c08ed8273e220f3c298444c7d5be8cb02e4b</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:55:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-deportation-project-72-journalists-investigate-us-treatment-of-migrants-1--dea57e7ef702.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-deportation-project-72-journalists-investigate-us-treatment-of-migrants-1" /><summary type="html">Under secretive deals with countries across Africa and Latin America, the Trump administration has deported thousands of migrants to countries they had never previously visited. Of the 25,000 deportations documented by reporters, the vast majority were sent across the border to Mexico. One of the journalists who investigated the story, Sofía Álvarez Jurado, explains how these people are forced across the borders to Mexico and what happens to them once they arrive.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron says talks with Trump on Ukraine, Red Sea were 'constructive'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5147918e3bee0ebb32a5077108550685f3791705af21b1eaea8407c6fa61766e</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T06:36:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-trump-to-meet-macron-in-new-york-before-un-general-assembly--0de11875e136.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-trump-to-meet-macron-in-new-york-before-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said Monday he had a “very good” and “constructive” discussion with US President Donald Trump on Ukraine and Red Sea security during talks in New York.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Third-country removals: Trump’s deportation policy by the numbers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8a15fad783bec4be3c470301e3c2529bc2ee643d7302bfe124077132e0bc625</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T05:04:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-third-country-removals-trump-deportation-policy-numbers--6d700771bc51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-third-country-removals-trump-deportation-policy-numbers" /><summary type="html">Since January 2025, the Trump administration has deported more than 25,000 people to so-called third countries – places that are not their countries of origin. Working with a consortium of 26 international media outlets, Forbidden Stories and FRANCE 24 used open-source information and data gathered by NGOs to map these deportations. Our investigation shines a light on the scale of this mass campaign that is being carried out under the cover of darkness.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>ICE, Trump and Africa: Secret deals, broken lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:356d41e0c773f64cc3e8f2e204619f584206d2b8565466729142b598f34bb222</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T05:00:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260921-ice-trump-and-africa-secret-deals-broken-lives--a4dce10e3903.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260921-ice-trump-and-africa-secret-deals-broken-lives" /><summary type="html">For this edition of Reporters+, Karina Chabour investigated the dark side of US President Donald Trump’s immigration policy: How ICE deports immigrants to so-called third countries in Africa, far from the United States and often far from their countries of origin.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>US, China discuss opening an AI communication channel ahead of Trump-Xi summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d83e809e434784d0de20a148adfbddcc1b05658bc19e25e9035586252bc6be08</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T02:22:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-china-discuss-ai-safety-ahead-of-trump-xi-summit--f6aa3899454b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-china-discuss-ai-safety-ahead-of-trump-xi-summit" /><summary type="html">US and Chinese officials discussed creating a communication channel over potentially serious AI incidents during talks in New York on Sunday as the two sides sought progress on technology and trade ahead of this week’s summit between US President Donald Trump and his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>The Deportation Project: Inside the Trump administration's secret deals to expel people worldwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:175867e8ad5c1ebedd1e129fee8a4c9d4a1f729c4c989bb305a89c7e62720d55</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T17:08:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260920-the-deportation-project-inside-the-trump-administration-s-secret-deals-to-expel-people-worl--8f166565a178.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260920-the-deportation-project-inside-the-trump-administration-s-secret-deals-to-expel-people-worldwide" /><summary type="html">A consortium of 72 journalists from 26 media outlets coordinated by Forbidden Stories have been working on the Deportation Project for months. On Monday, we will take you inside the Trump administration's secret deals to expel people worldwide.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran calls Gaza war catastrophic after dropping Macklemore over pro-Palestinian comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cffd0b7d8f76046860e92395d5e4bbf92bda380154328c3abe2a584cecd0d7c8</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:57:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-war-catastrophic-after-dropping-macklemore-over-pro-palestinian-comments--d2197bc47b01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-war-catastrophic-after-dropping-macklemore-over-pro-palestinian-comments" /><summary type="html">English singer Ed Sheeran opened his first show since his opener Macklemore was dropped after making pro-Palestinian comments onstage. The move sparked controversy and prompted several other support acts to drop out of the tour, publishing statements citing their support for Palestinians. While some concert goers could be seen trying to sell their tickets on Saturday, others have voiced their support for the 'Shape of You' singer. Story by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Three media outlets barred from the White House over 'fake news'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16ace124d067522940cf028388b72009089065b005611763a8f4fa81e554f8e7</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:55:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/three-media-outlets-barred-from-the-white-house-over-fake-news--17d25c5dc65b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/three-media-outlets-barred-from-the-white-house-over-fake-news" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has suggested that more news outlets may be barred from the White House after he announced he was banning Politico, CNN and MS NOW. On Saturday, all three outlets said that the White House confiscated their teams' press passes; they have also hinted at legal action. The ban has come under sharp criticism from press freedom advocates, as Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>US and Denmark reach Greenland security deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:101823ca1e55c09313ac5f5ed1585f6d08b7b69566de60f5e65964e6a568a3b6</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:40:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal--0d08e05eec1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal" /><summary type="html">The US and Denmark have announced a deal on Greenland's security, resolving a diplomatic dispute sparked by President Donald Trump when he threatened to seize the semi-autonomous territory. The exact terms of the deal remain uncertain but it seems Denmark will maintain its sovereignty while the US will be able to develop a significant military presence on the island, and ban their adversaries from building their own bases on the island. Details by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentines protest Milei's austerity, demanding higher wages and public spending</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c90a4b15e0f596599595f2baf839947ea0e6c8611b287bd3aaf5081e348aecd</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:38:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/argentines-protest-milei-s-austerity-demanding-higher-wages-and-public-spending--b313c3b28766.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-protest-milei-s-austerity-demanding-higher-wages-and-public-spending" /><summary type="html">Tensions are boiling over in Argentina, where a massive wave of public anger is spilling onto the streets of the capital. Following months of aggressive economic reforms and rising household debt, hundreds took to the streets in a "March of Anger", targeting President Javier Milei's austerity agenda. Details by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico reporters blocked from White House after Trump ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e2029430f299fa8a39b5398f8e36a4bed97dafc4e25a314cc27a824e7cda072</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:02:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban--a8c3f3f48609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban" /><summary type="html">White House correspondents for CNN, MS NOW and Politico on Saturday were blocked from entering the US president's office and residence a day after President Donald Trump announced he was banning the three media outlets for what he called "fake news" coverage. News organisations and press freedom groups have slammed the move as unconstitutional.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Millions without power in Cuba as electrical grid collapses again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a24192c871fcf581f0b7f668124fa62fc3767d0766abd5f2c874eeba25e6c71</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:01:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/millions-without-power-in-cuba-as-electrical-grid-collapses-again--8d09cc02680d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/millions-without-power-in-cuba-as-electrical-grid-collapses-again" /><summary type="html">Cuba was plunged into its seventh massive blackout of the year on Friday. The island of over nine million people endures constant power cuts due to the poor state of its aging thermoelectric plants – but the situation has worsened significantly since January, when Washington imposed a de facto energy blockade on the island. Story by Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump claims son repaid Russian oligarch who funded wedding festivities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8553cb790021f93dd7a97ab574975993c6fb31f72d5beee5fc25969692e7bcd0</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities--ec19dbba0a0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that his eldest son had repaid a Kremlin-linked Russian businessman who funded two days of lavish wedding celebrations in the Bahamas, after the gift raised questions over foreign influence and ethics.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump bans three media outlets from the White House, accusing them of spreading 'fake news'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c0d639bf0aa298d3b056d0580c3939edf673cc9078d5108c1f85032bb37ef8e</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:53:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-bans-three-media-outlets-from-the-white-house-accusing-them-of-spreading-fake-news--728977f11446.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-bans-three-media-outlets-from-the-white-house-accusing-them-of-spreading-fake-news" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump announced Friday he is banning CNN, MS NOW and Politico from the White House, accusing all three outlets of spreading 'fake news'. The move is almost certain to face legal challenges, and has been denounced by press freedom advocates. The US president's relationship with media outlets has long been fraught, as Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scientists discover first new wild cat in more than 100 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c8ee764e7173100762afa23e91d1a5cf350e22c57ab782e589631e5ffb66bf7</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:44:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-scientists-discover-first-new-wild-cat-in-more-than-100-years--a1fa381b5177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-scientists-discover-first-new-wild-cat-in-more-than-100-years" /><summary type="html">Scientists have identified a previously unknown species of wild cat living at a wildlife sanctuary in Bolivia. The tiny, spotted feline had lived at the sanctuary for years before genetic analysis revealed it as the first new living wild cat species identified in more than a century.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Cuba hit with another nationwide blackout amid US fuel blockade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2457940d6f32ca4ce73ca7f9f5a995c45dd404d6d92600531fa0a09c007a7e1b</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:31:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cuba-s-power-grid-collapses-again-leaving-island-in-darkness--27a189638edf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cuba-s-power-grid-collapses-again-leaving-island-in-darkness" /><summary type="html">Cuba suffered a total blackout after the collapse of its electrical grid on Friday. The blackout is the latest of at least six partial or total grid collapses since the beginning of this year, as the island grapples with an ongoing US fuel blockade.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pop star Ed Sheeran calls situation in Gaza 'unjustifiable' amid controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7872e74ddd941cfc4d16c3c371456cf763eb0ad1b172d693d319d946ab2d064b</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T05:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-situation-unjustifiable-amid-controversy--0909b0ea7b72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-situation-unjustifiable-amid-controversy" /><summary type="html">Ed Sheeran called the situation in Gaza “catastrophic and unjustifiable” on Saturday, speaking out for the first time since a controversy erupted over his tour’s removal of US rapper Macklemore after he made pro-Palestinian comments.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
